# Byte-exact checkout. Must agree with the repository root .gitattributes.
#
# This file previously said `* text=auto eol=lf`, written for the standalone
# consciousness-indicator-battery repository, where normalizing line endings kept
# diffs sane across Windows and Linux.
#
# Inside ScientificDiscoveryLab that instruction is wrong, and it was silently
# breaking the root integrity check. manifest.json records the SHA-256 of exact
# file bytes, so forcing LF here means a Linux checkout of these nine files
# produces bytes the manifest does not account for, and
# tools/verify_manifest.py reports them as CHANGED.
#
# A nested .gitattributes overrides the root one for its whole subtree, so the
# root `* -text` could not win while this file said otherwise.
#
# The normalisation was never load-bearing here. The battery's recorded hashes
# are computed over in-memory canonical-JSON values, not over file bytes, so
# `* -text` changes no recorded result. The standalone repository keeps its own
# copy of its own .gitattributes and is unaffected by this one.
* -text